# For development: copy to `.env` and fill in. `vp dev` and `bun src/cli/index.ts …` read it, but
# the built binary never does; in production these are set in the environment (e.g. by
# /etc/swiftace.env, which `swiftace deploy` creates). Variables already set in the environment win
# over this file. Everything else, including the keys for login providers, Stripe, Turnstile,
# PostHog and OpenAI, is set by an admin at /manage/config.

# Postgres. Create the tables with `vp run db:migrate`.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/swiftace

# Long random strings, e.g. from `openssl rand -hex 32`. Changing JWT_SECRET_KEY signs everyone out;
# changing HASH_SECRET_KEY voids pending sign-in codes and links.
JWT_SECRET_KEY=
HASH_SECRET_KEY=

# Email (AWS SES), S3-compatible object storage and rich notebook preview settings are saved
# in /manage/config. `swiftace deploy` asks for the first admin email and missing SES settings.
# Without deploy, use `swiftace configure-integrations <file.json>` before signing in; see README.md.

# Read by `swiftace start` (and `vp run dev:preview`), shown with their defaults.
# PORT=4000
# HOST=                            every address
# PREVIEW_PORT=4100                0 turns the notebook preview server off
# PREVIEW_ALLOWED_PARENT_ORIGINS=  the site's origin, e.g. https://example.com (required when serving previews)
